      {
        "id": "lem-qft-example-four-dimensional-radial-measure",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Four-dimensional radial measure from two polar planes",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. For every radius $R>0$ and every\nnonnegative Borel function $\\varphi:[0,R]\\to[0,\\infty]$, with extended\nLebesgue integrals and the convention $0\\cdot\\infty=0$,\n$$ \\int_{\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^4:\\ |x|\\le R\\}}\\varphi(|x|)\\,d\\lambda_4(x) =2\\pi^2\\int_0^R\\varphi(r)r^3\\,dr. $$\nIn particular, the radial Jacobian and angular factor on a four-dimensional\nball are $r^3$ and $2\\pi^2$, respectively.",
        "deps": [
          "def-countable-choice",
          "lem-c-one-change-of-variables-for-nonnegative-borel-functions-via-radon-uniqueness",
          "prop-degenerate-boxes-and-coordinate-hyperplanes-are-lebesgue-null",
