      {
        "id": "ex-qftmath-x07",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "title": "Worked mathematical example B07 — subtraction and a factorial series",
        "statement": "In the QX09 subtraction choose $\\mu_R=\\mu$. Its subtracted coefficient tends\nto zero, while the positive bare integral grows quadratically:\n$I_\\Lambda/\\Lambda^2\\to1/(16\\pi^2)$. This zero is determined by the selected\nsubtraction scale and does not assert zero fluctuations or existence of a\ncontinuum theory. For the separate toy integral $F(\\lambda)$, every finite\ncoefficient $n!$ exists, but the formal series diverges for every\n$\\lambda>0$.",
        "deps": [
          "lem-qft-example-cutoff-integrals-and-series"
        ],
